“For the Argo Rollouts Canary implementation, we are targeting December for completion across all environments, including Production.

First, we will complete the DEV POC with Argo Rollouts, Istio traffic splitting and Prometheus-based AnalysisRun.

Then we will validate the complete canary flow in lower environments—10%, 25%, 50% and finally 100% traffic—with both successful and failure/rollback scenarios.

After that, we will integrate it with our existing GitLab, Helm and ArgoCD/ApplicationSet deployment flow and validate the GitOps ownership of the Istio VirtualService, because Argo Rollouts dynamically manages traffic weights.

Once the lower environments are stable, we will progressively onboard SIT/UAT/Pre-Prod and then Production. Production will additionally require approval, monitoring, rollback validation and controlled rollout planning.

The timeline is therefore mainly because we need environment-wise validation and production-grade testing, rather than just implementing the Rollout YAML.”

